  "type": "songs",
  "content": "<div class=\"page-links\">Pages: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/songs/love-me-do/\" class=\"post-page-numbers\"><span class=\"page-link\">1</span></a> <span class=\"post-page-numbers current\" aria-current=\"page\"><span class=\"page-link\">2</span></span></div><div id=\"ez-toc-container\" class=\"ez-toc-v2_0_89 ez-toc-wrap-right counter-hierarchy ez-toc-counter ez-toc-grey ez-toc-container-direction\"><div class=\"ez-toc-title-container\"><p class=\"ez-toc-title\" style=\"cursor:inherit\">Contents</p>\n<span class=\"ez-toc-title-toggle\"><a href=\"#\" class=\"ez-toc-pull-right ez-toc-btn ez-toc-btn-xs ez-toc-btn-default ez-toc-toggle\" aria-label=\"Toggle Table of Content\"><span class=\"ez-toc-js-icon-con\"><span class=\"\"><span class=\"eztoc-hide\" style=\"display:none;\">Toggle</span><span class=\"ez-toc-icon-toggle-span\"><svg style=\"fill: #999;color:#999\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" class=\"list-377408\" width=\"20px\" height=\"20px\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\"><path d=\"M6 6H4v2h2V6zm14 0H8v2h12V6zM4 11h2v2H4v-2zm16 0H8v2h12v-2zM4 16h2v2H4v-2zm16 0H8v2h12v-2z\" fill=\"currentColor\"></path></svg><svg style=\"fill: #999;color:#999\" class=\"arrow-unsorted-368013\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"10px\" height=\"10px\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" version=\"1.2\" baseProfile=\"tiny\"><path d=\"M18.2 9.3l-6.2-6.3-6.2 6.3c-.2.2-.3.4-.3.7s.1.5.3.7c.2.2.4.3.7.3h11c.3 0 .5-.1.7-.3.2-.2.3-.5.3-.7s-.1-.5-.3-.7zM5.8 14.7l6.2 6.3 6.2-6.3c.2-.2.3-.5.3-.7s-.1-.5-.3-.7c-.2-.2-.4-.3-.7-.3h-11c-.3 0-.5.1-.7.3-.2.2-.3.5-.3.7s.1.5.3.7z\"/></svg></span></span></span></a></span></div><nav><ul class='ez-toc-list ez-toc-list-level-1 eztoc-toggle-hide-by-default' ><li class='ez-toc-page-1 ez-toc-heading-level-2'><a class=\"ez-toc-link ez-toc-heading-1\" href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/songs/love-me-do/#Personnel\" >Personnel</a></li><li class='ez-toc-page-1 ez-toc-heading-level-2'><a class=\"ez-toc-link ez-toc-heading-2\" href=\"#In_the_studio\" >In the studio</a></li><li class='ez-toc-page-1 ez-toc-heading-level-2'><a class=\"ez-toc-link ez-toc-heading-3\" href=\"#Chart_success\" >Chart success</a></li></ul></nav></div><h2><span class=\"ez-toc-section\" id=\"In_the_studio\"></span>In the studio<span class=\"ez-toc-section-end\"></span></h2><p>The Beatles recorded &#8216;Love Me Do&#8217; over three sessions. The first was at their EMI audition on <a href=\"/1962/06/06/the-beatles-first-abbey-road-recording-session/\">6 June 1962</a>, featuring <a href=\"/people/pete-best/\">Pete Best</a> on drums.</p><div class=\"epyt-video-wrapper\"><iframe  id=\"_ytid_85555\"  width=\"580\" height=\"435\"  data-origwidth=\"580\" data-origheight=\"435\"  data-relstop=\"1\" src=\"https://www.youtube.com/embed/e3Oc67FdcpY?enablejsapi=1&#038;autoplay=0&#038;cc_load_policy=0&#038;cc_lang_pref=&#038;iv_load_policy=1&#038;loop=0&#038;rel=0&#038;fs=1&#038;playsinline=0&#038;autohide=2&#038;theme=dark&#038;color=red&#038;controls=1&#038;disablekb=0&#038;\" class=\"__youtube_prefs__  epyt-is-override  no-lazyload\" title=\"YouTube player\"  allow=\"fullscreen; accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share\" referrerpolicy=\"strict-origin-when-cross-origin\" allowfullscreen data-no-lazy=\"1\" data-skipgform_ajax_framebjll=\"\"></iframe></div><p>They returned to the song during the <a href=\"/1962/09/04/recording-how-do-you-do-it-love-me-do/\">4 September session</a>, where it was considered for release along with <a href=\"/songs/how-do-you-do-it/\">&#8216;How Do You Do It&#8217;</a>. The group tackled it again on <a href=\"/1962/09/11/recording-ps-i-love-you-love-me-do-please-please-me/\">11 September</a>, after which it was deemed good enough for release as a single.</p><p>Although <a href=\"/people/ringo-starr/\">Ringo Starr</a> had played drums on 4 September, <a href=\"/people/george-martin/\">George Martin</a> brought in a session drummer, Andy White, for the subsequent recording, and Starr was relegated to tambourine.</p><blockquote><div>On my first visit in September we just ran through some tracks for George Martin. We even did <a href=\"/songs/please-please-me/\">&#8216;Please Please Me&#8217;</a>. I remember that, because while we were recording it I was playing the bass drum with a maraca in one hand and a tambourine in the other. I think it&#8217;s because of that that George Martin used Andy White, the &#8216;professional&#8217;, when we went down a week later to record &#8216;Love Me Do&#8217;. The guy was previously booked, anyway, because of Pete Best. George didn&#8217;t want to take any more chances and I was caught in the middle.</p><p>I was devastated that George Martin had his doubts about me. I came down ready to roll and heard, &#8216;We&#8217;ve got a professional drummer.&#8217; He has apologised several times since, has old George, but it was devastating \u2013 I hated the bugger for years; I still don&#8217;t let him off the hook!</p></div></blockquote><div class=\"source\">Ringo Starr<br />\n<a href=\"https://geni.us/anthologypb\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><em>Anthology</em></a></div><p>The presence of the tambourine is the easiest way to distinguish the two recordings. Initial copies of the single had Starr on drums, though the Andy White version became the preferred version from the release of the <em>Beatles Hits</em> EP on <a href=\"/1963/09/06/uk-release-the-beatles-hits-ep/\">6 September 1963</a>. To consolidate the decision EMI destroyed the master tapes of the 4 September recording.</p><p>It is White&#8217;s version which appears on the <a href=\"/albums/please-please-me/\"><em>Please Please Me</em></a> album, though Starr&#8217;s drumming can be heard on <a href=\"/albums/past-masters/\"><em>Past Masters</em></a>. The recording featuring Pete Best appeared on <a href=\"/albums/anthology-1/\"><em>Anthology 1</em></a> in 1995.</p><blockquote><div>George got his way and Ringo didn&#8217;t drum on the first single. He only played tambourine.</p><p>I don&#8217;t think Ringo ever got over that. He had to go back up to Liverpool and everyone asked, &#8216;How did it go in the Smoke?&#8217; We&#8217;d say, &#8216;B-side&#8217;s good,&#8217; but Ringo couldn&#8217;t admit to liking the a-side, not being on it.</p></div></blockquote><div class=\"source\"><a href=\"/people/paul-mccartney/\">Paul McCartney</a><br />\n<a href=\"https://geni.us/anthologypb\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><em>Anthology</em></a></div><p>The relegation of Starr wasn&#8217;t the only change made by George Martin to the song.</p><blockquote><div>George Martin said, &#8216;Can anyone play harmonica? It would be rather nice. Couldn&#8217;t think of some sort of bluesy thing, could you, <a href=\"/people/john-lennon/\">John</a>?&#8217; John played a chromatic harmonica, not a Sonny Boy Williamson blues harmonica, more Max Geldray from the <em>Goon Show</em>\u2026</p><p>The lyrics crossed over the harmonica solo so I suddenly got thrown the big open line, &#8216;Love me do&#8217;, where everything stopped. Until that session John had always done it; I didn&#8217;t even know how to sing it. I&#8217;d never done it before. George Martin just said, &#8216;You take that line, John take the harmonica, you cross over, we&#8217;ll do it live&#8217;\u2026</p><p>I can still hear the nervousness in my voice! We were downstairs in number two studio and I remember looking up to the big window afterwards and George Martin was saying, &#8216;Jolly good.&#8217;</p></div></blockquote><div class=\"source\">Paul McCartney<br />\n<a href=\"https://geni.us/manyyearsfromnow\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><em>Many Years From Now</em></a>, Barry Miles</div><figure id=\"attachment_108833\" aria-describedby=\"caption-attachment-108833\" style=\"width: 800px\" class=\"wp-caption aligncenter\"><a href=\"/gallery/lyrics/lyrics-love-me-do_01/\" rel=\"attachment wp-att-108833\"><img data-lazyloaded=\"1\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,PHN2ZyB4bWxucz0iaHR0cDovL3d3dy53My5vcmcvMjAwMC9zdmciIHdpZHRoPSI4MDAiIGhlaWdodD0iODcxIiB2aWV3Qm94PSIwIDAgODAwIDg3MSI+PHJlY3Qgd2lkdGg9IjEwMCUiIGhlaWdodD0iMTAwJSIgZmlsbD0iI2NmZDRkYiIvPjwvc3ZnPg==\" decoding=\"async\" data-attachment-id=\"108833\" data-permalink=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/gallery/lyrics/lyrics-love-me-do_01/\" data-orig-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/lyrics-love-me-do_01.jpg\" data-orig-size=\"1440,1567\" data-comments-opened=\"1\" data-image-title=\"Paul McCartney&amp;#8217;s handwritten lyrics for Love Me Do\" data-image-description=\"\" data-image-caption=\"&lt;p&gt;Paul McCartney&amp;#8217;s handwritten lyrics for Love Me Do&lt;/p&gt;\n\" data-large-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/lyrics-love-me-do_01-882x960.jpg\" data-src=\"/wp/media/lyrics-love-me-do_01-882x960.jpg\" alt=\"Paul McCartney&#039;s handwritten lyrics for Love Me Do\" width=\"800\" height=\"871\" class=\"size-large wp-image-108833\" data-srcset=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/lyrics-love-me-do_01-882x960.jpg 882w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/lyrics-love-me-do_01-533x580.jpg 533w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/lyrics-love-me-do_01-184x200.jpg 184w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/lyrics-love-me-do_01-768x836.jpg 768w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/lyrics-love-me-do_01-1412x1536.jpg 1412w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/lyrics-love-me-do_01.jpg 1440w\" data-sizes=\"(max-width: 800px) 100vw, 800px\" /></a><figcaption id=\"caption-attachment-108833\" class=\"wp-caption-text\">Paul McCartney&#8217;s handwritten lyrics for Love Me Do</figcaption></figure><h2><span class=\"ez-toc-section\" id=\"Chart_success\"></span>Chart success<span class=\"ez-toc-section-end\"></span></h2><p>The &#8216;Love Me Do&#8217; single reached number 17 in the UK charts, with sales mainly concentrated in and around Liverpool.</p><div data-carousel-extra='{&quot;blog_id&quot;:1,&quot;permalink&quot;:&quot;https://www.beatlesbible.com/songs/love-me-do/&quot;}' id='gallery-1' class='gallery galleryid-191 gallery-columns-3 gallery-size-thumbnail'><figure class='gallery-item'><div class='gallery-icon portrait'>\n<a href='https://www.beatlesbible.com/gallery/releases/uk_love-me-do/'><img decoding=\"sync\" width=\"196\" height=\"200\" src=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/uk_love-me-do-196x200.jpg\" class=\"attachment-thumbnail size-thumbnail\" alt=\"Love Me Do single - United Kingdom\" srcset=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/uk_love-me-do-196x200.jpg 196w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/uk_love-me-do-569x580.jpg 569w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/uk_love-me-do-942x960.jpg 942w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/uk_love-me-do-768x783.jpg 768w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/uk_love-me-do-66x66.jpg 66w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/uk_love-me-do.jpg 1000w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 196px) 100vw, 196px\" data-attachment-id=\"10199\" data-permalink=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/gallery/releases/uk_love-me-do/\" data-orig-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/uk_love-me-do.jpg\" data-orig-size=\"1000,1019\" data-comments-opened=\"1\" data-image-title=\"Love Me Do single \u2013 United Kingdom\" data-image-description=\"\" data-image-caption=\"\" data-large-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/uk_love-me-do-942x960.jpg\" fetchpriority=\"high\"></a></div></figure><figure class='gallery-item'><div class='gallery-icon landscape'>\n<a href='https://www.beatlesbible.com/gallery/releases/usa_love_me_do/'><img data-lazyloaded=\"1\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,PHN2ZyB4bWxucz0iaHR0cDovL3d3dy53My5vcmcvMjAwMC9zdmciIHdpZHRoPSIyMDAiIGhlaWdodD0iMTk4IiB2aWV3Qm94PSIwIDAgMjAwIDE5OCI+PHJlY3Qgd2lkdGg9IjEwMCUiIGhlaWdodD0iMTAwJSIgZmlsbD0iI2NmZDRkYiIvPjwvc3ZnPg==\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"200\" height=\"198\" data-src=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/usa_love_me_do-200x198.jpg\" class=\"attachment-thumbnail size-thumbnail\" alt=\"Love Me Do single artwork - USA\" data-srcset=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/usa_love_me_do-200x198.jpg 200w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/usa_love_me_do-580x574.jpg 580w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/usa_love_me_do-960x949.jpg 960w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/usa_love_me_do-768x760.jpg 768w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/usa_love_me_do-66x66.jpg 66w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/usa_love_me_do.jpg 1000w\" data-sizes=\"(max-width: 200px) 100vw, 200px\" data-attachment-id=\"10253\" data-permalink=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/gallery/releases/usa_love_me_do/\" data-orig-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/usa_love_me_do.jpg\" data-orig-size=\"1000,989\" data-comments-opened=\"1\" data-image-title=\"Love Me Do single artwork \u2013 USA\" data-image-description=\"\" data-image-caption=\"\" data-large-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/usa_love_me_do-960x949.jpg\" /></a></div></figure><figure class='gallery-item'><div class='gallery-icon landscape'>\n<a href='https://www.beatlesbible.com/gallery/releases/norway_love_me_do/'><img data-lazyloaded=\"1\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,PHN2ZyB4bWxucz0iaHR0cDovL3d3dy53My5vcmcvMjAwMC9zdmciIHdpZHRoPSIyMDAiIGhlaWdodD0iMTkxIiB2aWV3Qm94PSIwIDAgMjAwIDE5MSI+PHJlY3Qgd2lkdGg9IjEwMCUiIGhlaWdodD0iMTAwJSIgZmlsbD0iI2NmZDRkYiIvPjwvc3ZnPg==\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"200\" height=\"191\" data-src=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/norway_love_me_do-200x191.jpg\" class=\"attachment-thumbnail size-thumbnail\" alt=\"Love Me Do single artwork - Norway\" data-srcset=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/norway_love_me_do-200x191.jpg 200w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/norway_love_me_do-580x553.jpg 580w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/norway_love_me_do-960x916.jpg 960w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/norway_love_me_do-768x733.jpg 768w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/norway_love_me_do.jpg 1000w\" data-sizes=\"(max-width: 200px) 100vw, 200px\" data-attachment-id=\"9849\" data-permalink=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/gallery/releases/norway_love_me_do/\" data-orig-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/norway_love_me_do.jpg\" data-orig-size=\"1000,954\" data-comments-opened=\"1\" data-image-title=\"Love Me Do single artwork \u2013 Norway\" data-image-description=\"\" data-image-caption=\"\" data-large-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/norway_love_me_do-960x916.jpg\" /></a></div></figure></div><blockquote><div>There were enough fans of The Beatles around because we were playing all over the Wirral, Cheshire, Manchester and Liverpool. We were quite popular, so the sales <em>were</em> real.</p><p>First hearing &#8216;Love Me Do&#8217; on the radio sent me shivery all over. It was the best buzz of all time. We knew it was going to be on Radio Luxembourg at something like 7.30 on Thursday night. I was in my house in Speke and we all listened in. That was great, but after having got to 17, I don&#8217;t recall what happened to it. It probably went away and died, but what it meant was that the next time we went to EMI, they were more friendly: &#8216;Oh, hello lads. Come in.&#8217;</p></div></blockquote><div class=\"source\"><a href=\"/people/george-harrison/\">George Harrison</a><br />\n<a href=\"https://geni.us/anthologypb\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><em>Anthology</em></a></div><p>There were persistent rumours that <a href=\"/people/brian-epstein/\">Brian Epstein</a> had bulk-bought around 10,000 copies to increase its chart ranking, but these remain unproven.</p><blockquote><div>The best thing was it came into the charts in two days and everybody thought it was a fiddle, because our manager&#8217;s stores sent in these returns and everybody down south though, &#8216;Ah-ha, he&#8217;s buying them himself or he&#8217;s just fiddling the charts.&#8217; But he wasn&#8217;t.</div></blockquote><div class=\"source\"><a href=\"/people/john-lennon/\">John Lennon</a>, 1963<br />\n<a href=\"https://geni.us/anthologypb\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><em>Anthology</em></a></div><p>A true stereo remix of &#8216;Love Me Do&#8217; was the b-side of The Beatles&#8217; final single, <a href=\"/songs/now-and-then/\">&#8216;Now And Then&#8217;</a>, released in November 2023.</p><p>&#8216;Love Me Do&#8217; had been de-mixed using Peter Jackson&#8217;s MAL (machine-assisted learning) AI, named after The Beatles&#8217; road manager <a href=\"/people/mal-evans/\">Mal Evans</a>. The technology was first used in the 2021 documentary <em>Get Back</em>.</p><div class=\"fab-forum-link\"><a href=\"/fab-forum/the-songs/love-me-do/\">Discuss &#8216;Love Me Do&#8217; on the Fab Forum \u00bb</a></div><div class=\"wp-post-navigation\"><div class=\"wp-post-navigation-pre\"> <strong>Previous song:</strong> <a href=\"/songs/please-please-me/\">&#8216;Please Please Me&#8217;</a></div><div class=\"wp-post-navigation-next\"> <strong>Next song:</strong> <a href=\"/songs/ps-i-love-you/\">&#8216;PS I Love You&#8217;</a></div></div><div align=\"center\" style=\"clear:both;margin:15px 0;\"></div><div class=\"page-links\">Pages: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/songs/love-me-do/\" class=\"post-page-numbers\"><span class=\"page-link\">1</span></a> <span class=\"post-page-numbers current\" aria-current=\"page\"><span class=\"page-link\">2</span></span></div>",
  "scrapedAt": "2026-10-25"
}